Here's the full item-item collaborative filtering process:

Step 1 — Load data

u.item → movie details (ID, title, genres)
u.data → user ratings (user ID, item ID, rating)

Step 2 — Create user-item matrix (pivot table)

Rows = movies, Columns = users, Values = ratings
fill_value=0 for unrated movies
This gives each movie a "profile" of how all users rated it

Step 3 — Compute cosine similarity between items

Compares every movie's rating vector against every other movie
Result: 1682 x 1682 matrix (movie vs movie)
Similarity is based on how similarly users rated two movies
This is computed once and is the same for all users

Step 4 — For a given user, separate rated vs unrated movies

rated_movies → movies the user has rated (+ their ratings)
unrated_movies → movies the user hasn't rated (rating = 0)


Step 5 — Predict ratings for each unrated movie

For each unrated movie, get its similarity with the user's rated movies
Predicted rating = sim.dot(rated_movies) / sum(|sim|)
This is a weighted average — more similar movies influence the prediction more
Step 6 — Sort and recommend

Sort predicted ratings highest first
Top N movies = recommendations for that user
